hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18149","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me, from Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ansari, then of Banu Harithah, that he informed him that he was a governor over al-Yamamah, and that Marwan wrote to him that Muawiyah had written to him: Any man stolen from has most right to it for its price wherever he finds it. He said: So I wrote to Marwan that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged that if the one who bought it from the one who stole it is not suspect, its owner is given a choice: if he wishes, the one stolen from takes it for its price, and if he wishes, he pursues his thief. He said: And Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with them, judged likewise."
"18150","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: I asked Ata, and mentioned likewise. He said: I heard it said: Take your property wherever you find it. And Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me that Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ansari, then of Banu Harithah, informed him that he was a governor over al-Yamamah, and mentioned its meaning."
"18151","Hawdhah ibn Khalifah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to me that Usayd ibn Hudayr ibn Simak narrated to him, he said: Muawiyah wrote to Marwan ibn al-Hakam: If a man is stolen from, and mentioned the hadith."
